[32;1m[1;3mQuestion: A fund manager holds a portfolio of 6 assets and is considering using 120 European option types for hedging. Each option’s per-contract cost, delta, gamma, vega, and trading limits are given in OptionCharacteristics.csv. The underlying asset(s) each option refers to are given in Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv, with A[i,j]=1 if option i references asset j and 0 otherwise. (Note: some options may reference more than one asset.)

Variables:
Let $x_i$ be the integer number of contracts (positive for buy/long, negative for sell/short) for option $i$, $i=1,\dots,120$.

Objective:
Minimize total hedging cost:
$$
\min \sum_{i=1}^{120} \text{Cost}[i] \cdot |x_i|
$$

Subject to:

For each Greek $G \in \{\Delta,\Gamma,\text{Vega}\}$, the net portfolio exposure after hedging must satisfy:
$$
\left| G_{\text{initial}} + \sum_{i=1}^{120} \sum_{j=1}^{6} G[i] \cdot A[i,j] \cdot x_i \right| \leq \text{Tolerance}_G
$$

Where:
• $G_{\text{initial}}$ is the initial exposure for that Greek (given).
• $G[i]$ is the per-contract Greek exposure of option $i$ (from OptionCharacteristics.csv).
• $A[i,j]$ is from Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv.
• $\text{Tolerance}_G$ is the band for each risk metric (given).

Trading limits:
$$
\text{MaxShort}[i] \leq x_i \leq \text{MaxLong}[i], \quad i=1,\dots,120
$$

Data provided:
• OptionCharacteristics.csv: Option, Cost, Delta, Gamma, Vega, MaxLong, MaxShort
• Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv: binary matrix (120 × 6) showing which option references which asset (A[i,j])
• Initial net Delta = 0.25, Gamma = 0.08, Vega = 0.17
• Risk band tolerances: $|\Delta| \le 0.06$, $|\Gamma| \le 0.05$, $|\text{Vega}| \le 0.07$

Task:
Find the optimal integer positions $x_i,\ i=1,\dots,120$ that minimize total hedging cost, such that all risk exposures after hedging are within their respective bands, while respecting per-option trading limits and using the asset-reference information in the constraints.

Thought: Retrieve all data from OptionCharacteristics.csv and Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv, preserving identifiers, coefficients, and source order. Use the initial exposures and tolerances as given.

Action: CSVQA
Action Input: Retrieve all data from OptionCharacteristics.csv and Option_AssetReferenceMatrix.csv, preserving source order and all identifiers and coefficients.
